<!--
  The small icon Android draws in the status bar and beside the notification: Zuno's Z.

  A flat white silhouette on transparency, and it has to be. Android throws away every colour in
  this icon and redraws it as one solid shape, tinted with whatever `color` the notification
  carries — so full-colour artwork arrives as a featureless white blob. That is what happened when
  the launcher icon was used here.

  Drawn rather than traced from the app icon, because there is no Zuno artwork in this project: the
  launcher icon is still Flutter's own blue logo. Replace this with the real mark when there is
  one, keeping it a single white path on transparency.

  Geometry: thick bars top and bottom with a diagonal between, on the 24dp grid Android expects.
  Heavy on purpose — at status-bar size a thin letterform closes up into a smudge.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="24dp"
    android:height="24dp"
    android:viewportWidth="24"
    android:viewportHeight="24"
    android:tint="#FFFFFFFF">
    <path
        android:fillColor="#FFFFFFFF"
        android:pathData="M5,4 H19 V7 L10.5,17 H19 V20 H5 V17 L13.5,7 H5 Z" />
</vector>
